<title>UK: Midland News firm on report of MGN bid plan.</title>
<headline>Midland News firm on report of MGN bid plan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Midland Independent Newspapers Plc nudged higher by early afternoon on Monday after a weekend press report said Mirror Group Newspapers Plc was considering a bid.</p>
<p>Midland shares were up 1-1/2p at 147 by 1438 GMT, while MGN was down 1p at 200.</p>
<p>The Mail on Sunday newspaper said MGN was mulling a 250 million stg bid for Midland, which owns the Birmingham Post and other titles.</p>
<p>A spokesman for MGN said the company's policy was to never comment on market speculation. No-one at Midland was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
